Description:

When parsing a message, Cyrus now handles header fields with empty values
safely.  Previously, an empty address header or a Received header with
nothing after its last semicolon could make Cyrus read, and in some cases
write, memory beyond the end of the header value while delivering or
parsing a message.  Reported by interpolwantme.  This is CYR-3529 and
CYR-3587.

Reported by "interpolwantme".

